<title>RUSSIA: Red October raises 1996 dividend to 1,900 rbls.</title>
<headline>Red October raises 1996 dividend to 1,900 rbls.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian chocolate maker Red October is raising its 1996 dividend to 1,900 roubles per ordinary share from 1,800 roubles paid on 1995 results, President Anatoly Daursky told a news conference on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Red October's full name in Russian is AOOT Moskovskaya Konditerskaya Fabrika Krasny Oktyabr.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
